**Truth defined first** | **Translation, not reimplementation** | **Disagreements become bugs**

{{ orgIntro(org) }}

**Most Figma kits retell the design system's story in a second language.** A design team draws the components, engineers build them, and the two versions drift because nothing ties one to the other. Every correction has to be made twice, by different people, from memory.

**Mangrove's Figma library is a translation instead.** The story was already told: in the structured content schemas that define what a component is made of, in the design tokens that define how it looks in each of UNDRR's five brands, and in [Storybook](https://mangrove.undrr.org/), where the two combine into working web patterns. I built a Figma plugin that reads all three and rebuilds the patterns as a 297-variant library across 396 symbols.

**Translating is still work, but it is not a different story.** When Figma disagreed with one of its sources, that was a bug with an address, not a matter of taste.

## Where did the truth come from?

**We had already done the hard part, for a different reason.** UNDRR syndicates content across its websites, and syndication only works when every site agrees what a card, a hero or a landing page is *made of*: which fields it has, which are optional, how long they can run. That is structure, not appearance, and the team had settled it before Figma was in scope. (I've written about this as [Mangrove being a content architecture that happens to ship a design system](/posts/20260327-content-architecture-shipping-container/).)

**The design tokens are the second source of truth, and a peer.** I merged the tokens from UNDRR, PreventionWeb, MCR2030, DELTA Resilience and IRP into one engine of 540 tokens. 471 of them, 87.2%, are a shared core; the remaining 69 are where the brands differ: colour, radius, a soft surface here, hero spacing there.

**Neither source depends on the other.** A schema says nothing about colour, and a token says nothing about whether a card has an image. Because the content structure was well understood, design could become an **enablement layer** on top of it rather than the place where components get defined.

