## How does Figma triangulate between all three?

**Figma comes from a different lineage.** Its component model (Auto Layout, variables, variant properties) does not map one-to-one onto HTML and CSS, so a kit copied from Storybook screenshots inherits the look and loses the structure.

**So the plugin reads all three sources, not just the nearest one.** It takes field lists and presets from the structured content schemas, binds values to Figma variables generated from the tokens, and uses the Storybook patterns as the layout reference. I wrote it with AI coding agents. That worked because the input was structured data with a checkable answer: the agents traced tokens through the repository and generated construction recipes, and every recipe could be compared against its sources.

**Nothing in the library is invented in Figma.** A designer switching the Book Card from `Default` to `NoImage` is choosing a preset the schema already allows, not drawing a new variant.

